--TEST--
an in-process request's `captures` reach `Core\Request::mount()->captures()` in order beside its `mount`, and `captures` without a `mount` or keyed by name throws a `LogicError` — `rule:testing/in-process-request`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Test::request
//
// A mount's prefix and its pattern's captures are one row, so a test states
// both or the prefix alone. The root has no pattern, so captures with no
// mount describe a request no server could send.
//
// The `catch (LogicError ...)` is the parent: there is no request in its run.
try {
    Core\Request\Mount $mount = Core\Request::mount();
    echo "prefix ", $mount->prefix(), " captures ", Core\Arr::count($mount->captures());
    foreach ($mount->captures() as tainted string $part) {
        echo " [", $part, "]";
    }
} catch (LogicError $noRequest) {
    var $tenant = Core\Test::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/orders", {mount: "/acme/eu", captures: ["Acme", "eu"]});
    echo $tenant->body(), "\n";

    var $plain = Core\Test::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/orders", {mount: "/shop"});
    echo $plain->body(), "\n";

    var $root = Core\Test::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/orders");
    echo $root->body(), "\n";

    try {
        Core\Test::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/orders", {captures: ["Acme"]});
    } catch (LogicError $noMount) {
        echo $noMount->message, "\n";
    }

    try {
        Core\Test::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/orders", {mount: "/acme", captures: ["tenant" => "Acme"]});
    } catch (LogicError $keyed) {
        echo $keyed->message, "\n";
    }
}
--EXPECT--
prefix /acme/eu captures 2 [Acme] [eu]
prefix /shop captures 0
prefix  captures 0
Core\Test::request(): `captures` needs a `mount` — the captures are parts of the prefix a request came in under, and the root has no pattern to capture
Core\Test::request(): `captures` must be a list — `{1}` is its first entry, so a key names nothing
